# erlinit.config for Xiaomi Pad 6S Pro (sheng)
#
# erlinit auto-detects the OTP release under /srv/erlang (see
# https://github.com/nerves-project/erlinit#release-setup) and prefers the
# ERTS bundled inside the release itself, matching this project's
# `include_erts: &Nerves.Release.erts/0` release config - no --release-path
# or --boot needed.
#
# Rebooting (not hanging) on Erlang VM exit/fatal error is already erlinit's
# default behavior, so not spelled out explicitly here. No --hostname-pattern
# / --uniqueid-exec either (would need the untested `boardid` package) -
# mdns_lite already advertises the fixed "nerves.local" name regardless of
# hostname (see config/target.exs), which is enough to ssh in.

# Boot signals (before Erlang VM starts)
#
# LED blink: 10 rapid blinks + 1 second hold = erlinit is running, userspace alive
#   If you see LED blinks, the kernel booted and erlinit started successfully.
#   No LED blinks = stuck in kernel or bootloader, never reached userspace.
#
# Audio beep: 3 beeps @ 1000Hz = audio subsystem working
#   If LED blinks but no beeps, audio failed (driver/firmware issue).
#   If both: device is alive and working, waiting for Erlang to start.

-c /usr/bin/boot-led-blink.sh
-c /usr/bin/boot-beep.sh